---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import DataTable from '../components/DataTable.astro';
import { chapters } from '../data/site';

const ch = chapters.find((c) => c.id === 'finance')!;
const lead =
  'To ensure a comprehensive and resilient financial overview for ICPS28, the following section outlines our financial planning structured across two distinct attendance scenarios: a 500 participants model and a 400 participants model.';
---

<Layout title={ch.title} description="ICPS 2028 project proposal — Finance chapter." chapter={ch.id}>
  <header class="chapter-head">
    <p class="chapter-head__kicker">Chapter {String(ch.num).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
    <h1>{ch.title}</h1>
    <p class="chapter-head__lead">{lead}</p>
  </header>

  <article class="prose">
    <p>
      In line with standard event management practices, each attendance scenario features two
      separate budgetary paths:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Plan A (provisional budget):</strong> This represents our optimal operating
        framework, designed to deliver the highest quality experience across all event components.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Plan B (fallback budget):</strong> This functions as our emergency contingency
        model, designed to ensure the financial viability and secure execution of the event under a
        more constrained economic framework.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The primary operational difference between the two configurations lies in a strategic
      reduction of catering provisions (specifically regarding the frequency and scale of coffee
      breaks, lunches, and dinners) and a measured downsizing of communication and branding
      materials, such as speaker and participant prizes.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Provisional budget (Plan A) - 500 participants</h2>

      <h4>Accomodation</h4>
      <DataTable
        headers={['Group', 'Num. of People', 'Num. of Nights', 'Price / Night (€)', 'Total (€)']}
        rows={[
          ['Participants', 500, 6, '35.00', '105,000.00'],
          ['Guest Speakers', 10, 1, '100.00', '1,000.00'],
        ]}
        foot={['Subtotal', '', '', '', '106,000.00']}
      />

      <h4>Transportation</h4>
      <DataTable
        headers={['Transport', 'Num. of People', 'Price (€)', 'Total (€)']}
        rows={[
          ['City ticket - Milano', 500, '15.50', '7,750.00'],
          ['City ticket - Torino', 500, '12.50', '6,250.00'],
          ['Shuttle OaTO', 80, '6.25', '500.00'],
          ['Guest speakers', 10, '200.00', '2,000.00'],
          ['Excursions', 500, '36.30', '18,150.00'],
        ]}
        foot={['Subtotal', '', '', '34,650.00']}
      />

      <h4>Food</h4>
      <DataTable
        headers={['Meal', 'Num. of People', 'Num. of Meals', 'Price / Meal (€)', 'Total (€)']}
